Read ALL four v4 verdicts, the FULL v5 design and its diff from v4, the oracle README, the oracle source/test, and check claims against actual Java and current Go. v5 answers the v4 NAKs: capability refusals poison the record context through a keyed commit check (so catch-and-commit cannot commit; replaces the unbuildable pre-buffer admission and covers the sliding window and update/queued compound effects); an admission matrix derived from the MEASURED knob-consumer golden (throw vs livelock vs silent degradation) and Java's real MUTABLE_OPTIONS, with deletes matching Java where Java succeeds; the vector Update adopts the existing common-entry filter; insert admission at enqueue and terminal (non-retried) capability errors; each retry owner keeps its own limit schedule with a shared prefix-targeted hand-off at limit 1 using snapshot count/lease reads, the build's session id as lease owner, foreign-lease backoff, and a single progress rule on the blocked cluster; the hard cap applied in both maintenance modes; kept empty merge cluster re-armed through the undersized-merge rule; executor changes scoped to IndexTypeVector with SPFresh continuations unaffected; cooperative join rule; full lock order; pass-2 stats rebuilt; collapse helper takes stats/states as inputs; capacity errors non-poisoning with the record staying unindexed as in Java. Challenge sufficiency and interactions with the rest of the design, not only whether the requested words appear. Distinguish measured target facts (oracle) from remaining source hypotheses.
Preserved boundaries: GuardiANN executes in merger-supplied transactions (no invented child runner); SPFresh independent algorithms/LIRE; approved raw/nullable-array/scalar/sort extensions; C++ 7.3.77; format max 15/default 14; Lucene is separate upgrade-wide work, not Go TEXT; WS-D cannot complete with a refusal or fake backend.
Actual reviewer gate run via `claude -p` (model opus = claude-opus-5-5, effort xhigh) under a read-only tool policy (Read/Grep/Glob plus read-only git/grep/sed Bash; no Edit/Write). The owner authorized this substitution for the exhausted Codex account. No tests/probes/mutations/edits/staging/commits/push/CI/PR/publication/operational changes. Return ACK or NAK, the exact tree and design hash, and actionable findings with source line references ordered by severity. Incomplete review is not ACK. Under 900 words unless needed.

Apply the virtual Linus Torvalds code quality lens: logic holes, races, cancellation/lifetime ownership, test vacuity, incomplete fixes, duplicate mechanisms and maintainability.
